  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Adaptation in the Age of Media Convergence (2025), published by Taylor & Francis, has been cited 6 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 3,364 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Adaptation in the Age of Media Convergence by Johannes Fehrle and Werner Schäfke-Zell was published by Taylor & Francis in 2025. Conceptually, the work connects to Technological convergence, Negotiation, Adaptation (eye), Convergence (economics) and Perspective (graphical).</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 6 citations. Notable citing venues include PLoS ONE and Adaptation. The citing works include 2 journal articles and 1 dissertation. They come from 2 countries, led by the United Kingdom and the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 3,364 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Peace, Justice and strong institutions among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
